(6459699, 959422, 96800, '<td valign="top">I love this photo! Great subject matter and colour. I can easily imagine seeing it in the pages of NG.</td>', 'I love this photo! Great subject matter and colour. I can easily imagine seeing it in the pages of NG.', '2011-07-03 12:04:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459701, 959628, 96800, '<td valign="top">Fantastic photo.</td>', 'Fantastic photo.', '2011-07-03 12:05:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459706, 959244, 96800, '<td valign="top">The focus and detail really bring out the character of the subject for me.</td>', 'The focus and detail really bring out the character of the subject for me.', '2011-07-03 12:07:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459739, 959777, 39880, '<td valign="top">A nice picture for the family album, but not sure about NG.</td>', 'A nice picture for the family album, but not sure about NG.', '2011-07-03 13:01:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459740, 959578, 39880, '<td valign="top">This has some nice colors, but I think the focus could be sharper.</td>', 'This has some nice colors, but I think the focus could be sharper.', '2011-07-03 13:02:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459741, 959396, 39880, '<td valign="top">Composition, light, and color look good.  But to me it looks a bit soft.</td>', 'Composition, light, and color look good.  But to me it looks a bit soft.', '2011-07-03 13:03:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459742, 959785, 39880, '<td valign="top">A nice scene.  I like the silhouette.  However, his head blends into the background.</td>', 'A nice scene.  I like the silhouette.  However, his head blends into the background.', '2011-07-03 13:05:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459837, 959752, 48228, '<td valign="top">AWESOME..... from shez <br/>The BLUE I THINK</td>', 'AWESOME..... from shez The BLUE I THINK', '2011-07-03 14:00:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459863, 959665, 108580, '<td valign="top">This is real DPC eye candy, pushed processing, dramatic clouds and sky, good composition but lacking in saturation and whilst normally I''d give this a high score, NG are very anti-PP. Dodging, burning and cropping or a blended multi shot HDR is all they allow, which due to the lack of staggered clouds I fear this has been Topaz''d or the like. Tough call.</td>', 'This is real DPC eye candy, pushed processing, dramatic clouds and sky, good composition but lacking in saturation and whilst normally I''d give this a high score, NG are very anti-PP. Dodging, burning and cropping or a blended multi shot HDR is all they allow, which due to the lack of staggered clouds I fear this has been Topaz''d or the like. Tough call.', '2011-07-03 14:30:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459868, 959766, 108580, '<td valign="top">Unusual POV which is common for NG. Finding a new way to look at old subjects. Without an article to support this image I''m not sure it would be used as the overall image is not telling me a story on it''s own.</td>', 'Unusual POV which is common for NG. Finding a new way to look at old subjects. Without an article to support this image I''m not sure it would be used as the overall image is not telling me a story on it''s own.', '2011-07-03 14:33:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459887, 959562, 3102, '<td valign="top">Very, very nice!  Definitely has ribbon potential.</td>', 'Very, very nice!  Definitely has ribbon potential.', '2011-07-03 14:48:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459891, 959692, 108580, '<td valign="top">I like this. It has form, colour, 3 dimensional elements. Title is NG style. I would have shot it from a higher POV to get the top rim of the vase flat and parallel to your frame, and not falling off to the right. As it is the vase  looks tilted to the right and not vertical. The BG is not totally black, and it doesn''t HAVE to be, as it could be in a gallery with a cloth BG that itself is not 100% black. There is a small reflection highlight from a nearby light source, not bad but I might have tried to diffuse that. Publishable? A fair chance.</td>', 'I like this. It has form, colour, 3 dimensional elements. Title is NG style. I would have shot it from a higher POV to get the top rim of the vase flat and parallel to your frame, and not falling off to the right. As it is the vase  looks tilted to the right and not vertical. The BG is not totally black, and it doesn''t HAVE to be, as it could be in a gallery with a cloth BG that itself is not 100% black. There is a small reflection highlight from a nearby light source, not bad but I might have tried to diffuse that. Publishable? A fair chance.', '2011-07-03 14:54:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459893, 959443, 108580, '<td valign="top">Great shot. I shot one a few years back and battled to identify it. That means that you have at least spent some time trying to identify your subject, a good NG trait. The title has helped the viewer identify the insect and get an education about it! I think you used a ring flash or off camera flash at least and this is not unheard of in NG but it has washed out the image a little. Still a good, thoughtful effort with decent focus on the head and everything is visible and well composed. Publishable? Sure.</td>', 'Great shot. I shot one a few years back and battled to identify it. That means that you have at least spent some time trying to identify your subject, a good NG trait. The title has helped the viewer identify the insect and get an education about it! I think you used a ring flash or off camera flash at least and this is not unheard of in NG but it has washed out the image a little. Still a good, thoughtful effort with decent focus on the head and everything is visible and well composed. Publishable? Sure.', '2011-07-03 14:57:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459896, 959243, 108580, '<td valign="top">BW are seldom used at NG, certainly less of it in the past decade or so. It''s risky to use it in an NG challenge. Most people EXPECT a colourful image of a yawning lion or a breaching whale. I like the image. It''s minimalist with a huge expanse of negative space. But what story is it telling? I''m left empty. Have nothing to tie it in with, other than if it is referred to in the text, article it would be associated with. Publishable? Not on it''s own merits I don''t think, sorry.</td>', 'BW are seldom used at NG, certainly less of it in the past decade or so. It''s risky to use it in an NG challenge. Most people EXPECT a colourful image of a yawning lion or a breaching whale. I like the image. It''s minimalist with a huge expanse of negative space. But what story is it telling? I''m left empty. Have nothing to tie it in with, other than if it is referred to in the text, article it would be associated with. Publishable? Not on it''s own merits I don''t think, sorry.', '2011-07-03 15:04:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459898, 959394, 108580, '<td valign="top">Egypt, Abyssinia, Greek temple? All possible. Usable 3D POV. The lighting, I''m not a fan. Rather than a direct flash from the right seemingly flat on, or maybe a pop-up I''d have used off camera flash from the left of the camera just touching the relief, adding some light/dark differences to make the faces pop out of the image. Hard if you only have 3 seconds and the tour guide is rushing you on a bit I know...I think the image could be usable if you had an explorer in pith helmet pointing to a face with a cane.</td>', 'Egypt, Abyssinia, Greek temple? All possible. Usable 3D POV. The lighting, I''m not a fan. Rather than a direct flash from the right seemingly flat on, or maybe a pop-up I''d have used off camera flash from the left of the camera just touching the relief, adding some light/dark differences to make the faces pop out of the image. Hard if you only have 3 seconds and the tour guide is rushing you on a bit I know...I think the image could be usable if you had an explorer in pith helmet pointing to a face with a cane.', '2011-07-03 15:07:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459904, 959658, 108580, '<td valign="top">Well lit, including the street, so exposure is acceptable. Title fits an NG story.  I would have chosen a lower POV and not had half a fluorescent tube and half a clock. The empty chairs and idle barber are indicative of the story.</td>', 'Well lit, including the street, so exposure is acceptable. Title fits an NG story.  I would have chosen a lower POV and not had half a fluorescent tube and half a clock. The empty chairs and idle barber are indicative of the story.', '2011-07-03 15:20:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459905, 959394, 27515, '<td valign="top">I would have liked this photo a little more if the lighting displayed more depth in the carvings.</td>', 'I would have liked this photo a little more if the lighting displayed more depth in the carvings.', '2011-07-03 15:22:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459907, 959827, 27515, '<td valign="top">I love the eyes!</td>', 'I love the eyes!', '2011-07-03 15:22:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459910, 959742, 27515, '<td valign="top">My favorite in this challenge!</td>', 'My favorite in this challenge!', '2011-07-03 15:24:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459911, 959347, 108580, '<td valign="top">Great work, typical classic photographic technique, with leading lines, smooth sky, gradations, humans, POV, composition. Classic and publishable if tied into an article, well done. I''d just get rid of the border if submitting to NG...</td>', 'Great work, typical classic photographic technique, with leading lines, smooth sky, gradations, humans, POV, composition. Classic and publishable if tied into an article, well done. I''d just get rid of the border if submitting to NG...', '2011-07-03 15:25:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459912, 959369, 108580, '<td valign="top">It''s a nice attempt. I think either over cropped or over processed. The composition leads my eye back to the well lit shell and I think the head and antennae are far more important, as is the water drop. I don''t think it would be snapped up by NG, sorry.</td>', 'It''s a nice attempt. I think either over cropped or over processed. The composition leads my eye back to the well lit shell and I think the head and antennae are far more important, as is the water drop. I don''t think it would be snapped up by NG, sorry.', '2011-07-03 15:27:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459913, 959244, 101668, '<td valign="top">Wonderful picture, it even looks endangered</td>', 'Wonderful picture, it even looks endangered', '2011-07-03 15:29:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459914, 959607, 108580, '<td valign="top">Of course NG have shot, written about architecture a lot over the years. This has a great aspect and a lot to look at. Half the fun of NG images, lots to look at. What is it though? A church, a public space? Not clear! No real story. Difficult exposure and I don''t think you''ve done much if any PP. Good for you to stick to NG rules. I''d maybe have dropped EV by -0.3 or -0.5 just to give a bit more contrast and saturation. Still a worthy image and I''ve seen worse. The title is a bit odd, perhaps not typical NG. Print it!</td>', 'Of course NG have shot, written about architecture a lot over the years. This has a great aspect and a lot to look at. Half the fun of NG images, lots to look at. What is it though? A church, a public space? Not clear! No real story. Difficult exposure and I don''t think you''ve done much if any PP. Good for you to stick to NG rules. I''d maybe have dropped EV by -0.3 or -0.5 just to give a bit more contrast and saturation. Still a worthy image and I''ve seen worse. The title is a bit odd, perhaps not typical NG. Print it!', '2011-07-03 15:32:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459915, 959429, 121949, '<td valign="top">What a lucky break in the clouds. I''m glad this is doing well for you.</td>', 'What a lucky break in the clouds. I''m glad this is doing well for you.', '2011-07-03 15:37:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459916, 959464, 108580, '<td valign="top">Very early underwater NG images had this very odd CA and weird colour. Either the film of the day or the paper/print process. I remember it well. Maybe the need for flash too had an effect. This so screams NG underwater photography of old. In this case it might be in an aquarium, through a 2" thick laminated glass and the laminate added that green tinge and light diffraction. So what. Print it. They looked like this for years.</td>', 'Very early underwater NG images had this very odd CA and weird colour. Either the film of the day or the paper/print process. I remember it well. Maybe the need for flash too had an effect. This so screams NG underwater photography of old. In this case it might be in an aquarium, through a 2" thick laminated glass and the laminate added that green tinge and light diffraction. So what. Print it. They looked like this for years.', '2011-07-03 15:37:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459918, 959774, 108580, '<td valign="top">That''s so Dr Achoo it isn''t funny...and if it isn''t I have to cover my ass so well done if you aren''t he :) I love it. You can''t ask for better in all departments. Background is superb. A dream. The light is exceptional, the focus on the drops perfect. One niggle, the bugs head, by nature of his upright position, is not ideal and a tad hidden by the right antennae. Would NG use it? I think so. Now ditch the frame. It''s ghastly.</td>', 'That''s so Dr Achoo it isn''t funny...and if it isn''t I have to cover my ass so well done if you aren''t he :) I love it. You can''t ask for better in all departments. Background is superb. A dream. The light is exceptional, the focus on the drops perfect. One niggle, the bugs head, by nature of his upright position, is not ideal and a tad hidden by the right antennae. Would NG use it? I think so. Now ditch the frame. It''s ghastly.', '2011-07-03 15:42:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459921, 958555, 105569, '<td valign="top">Good picture ruined by an ugly border. My opinion still deserves a  7</td>', 'Good picture ruined by an ugly border. My opinion still deserves a  7', '2011-07-03 15:53:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459924, 959562, 108580, '<td valign="top">Super shot, more so because it''s a BiF AND it''s in focus. Technically difficult even with a multi-shot per second DSLR. You still need to be expecting it, to know it''s flight path, to pan, to frame. Publish it now! But only after you fix the typo :)</td>', 'Super shot, more so because it''s a BiF AND it''s in focus. Technically difficult even with a multi-shot per second DSLR. You still need to be expecting it, to know it''s flight path, to pan, to frame. Publish it now! But only after you fix the typo :)', '2011-07-03 15:59:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459925, 958555, 101668, '<td valign="top">Good picture ruined by the yellow border</td>', 'Good picture ruined by the yellow border', '2011-07-03 15:59:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459926, 958679, 101668, '<td valign="top">This is lovely</td>', 'This is lovely', '2011-07-03 15:59:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459928, 959844, 108580, '<td valign="top">Appealing image. Down to the bits of muck on the body. The huge OOF area to bottom right is distracting. If possible crop higher with more black above it''s head and less rock. Could then easily be used in NG.</td>', 'Appealing image. Down to the bits of muck on the body. The huge OOF area to bottom right is distracting. If possible crop higher with more black above it''s head and less rock. Could then easily be used in NG.', '2011-07-03 16:00:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459934, 958394, 52472, '<td valign="top">It''s exactly the type of wildlife shot which feels alive and puts the viewer right there. Therefore quite worthy of the National Geographic! The birds'' motion blur does it for me. The lighting is also great. Just the composition feels a bit wrong, I guess not enough space in front of the calf.</td>', 'It''s exactly the type of wildlife shot which feels alive and puts the viewer right there. Therefore quite worthy of the National Geographic! The birds'' motion blur does it for me. The lighting is also great. Just the composition feels a bit wrong, I guess not enough space in front of the calf.', '2011-07-03 16:20:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459941, 959231, 108580, '<td valign="top">Whilst it''s ''close'' I fear you have over cropped and in so doing lost definition, focus, sharpness. It''s also OE. NG also tend to name the subject in question, by common and scientific names or at least give some explanation about the shot. It''s unlikely this image would be published unless it''s a one of a kind, never seen before bird, and this is the only picture they got of it deep in some Amazonian jungle.</td>', 'Whilst it''s ''close'' I fear you have over cropped and in so doing lost definition, focus, sharpness. It''s also OE. NG also tend to name the subject in question, by common and scientific names or at least give some explanation about the shot. It''s unlikely this image would be published unless it''s a one of a kind, never seen before bird, and this is the only picture they got of it deep in some Amazonian jungle.', '2011-07-03 16:33:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459942, 959842, 108580, '<td valign="top">As before, I''d prefer to a see a steam train go over it :)<br/>It''s great. The slow shutter speed has naturally done wonders to this, the movement in the tourists, the soft curtain of water. As the subject of a story it could well be published but would need supporting text.</td>', 'As before, I''d prefer to a see a steam train go over it :)It''s great. The slow shutter speed has naturally done wonders to this, the movement in the tourists, the soft curtain of water. As the subject of a story it could well be published but would need supporting text.', '2011-07-03 16:35:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6459959, 959785, 101668, '<td valign="top">This is beautiful. The colours are unreal and sharpness exquisite.</td>', 'This is beautiful. The colours are unreal and sharpness exquisite.', '2011-07-03 17:31:49.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(6459967, 959494, 1073, '<td valign="top">NG is famous in color pics. yours ?</td>', 'NG is famous in color pics. yours ?', '2011-07-03 18:17:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460001, 958579, 125389, '<td valign="top">Not voting, but what a great shot.  He looks like I feel.  I hope you win...it is the best photo in this challenge.</td>', 'Not voting, but what a great shot.  He looks like I feel.  I hope you win...it is the best photo in this challenge.', '2011-07-03 19:06:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460041, 959628, 117037, '<td valign="top">It''s a big portion of meal...nice moment.</td>', 'It''s a big portion of meal...nice moment.', '2011-07-03 20:17:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460042, 959785, 117037, '<td valign="top">Lovely colors transition.</td>', 'Lovely colors transition.', '2011-07-03 20:18:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460044, 959665, 117037, '<td valign="top">Great scene...will be fabulous with a human touch.</td>', 'Great scene...will be fabulous with a human touch.', '2011-07-03 20:25:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460046, 959422, 117037, '<td valign="top">It''s not easy to decide the framing when doing a snapshot, I think composing the people on the door and square windows only will even greater, imho.</td>', 'It''s not easy to decide the framing when doing a snapshot, I think composing the people on the door and square windows only will even greater, imho.', '2011-07-03 20:35:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460047, 959196, 117037, '<td valign="top">Lovely soft tone.</td>', 'Lovely soft tone.', '2011-07-03 20:36:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460048, 959451, 117037, '<td valign="top">You should try framing w/o fence and bring out the houses as pov, imho.</td>', 'You should try framing w/o fence and bring out the houses as pov, imho.', '2011-07-03 20:36:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460049, 959429, 117037, '<td valign="top">Great pic.</td>', 'Great pic.', '2011-07-03 20:38:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460606, 958628, 108580, '<td valign="top">Beautiful work. Natural shot in natural environs. Nice light accentuation on the antlers and good exposure, DOF. There needs to be some engagement between the subject and the viewer, of which there is none. The border is common at DPC but not NG except where only one black frame is used generally at the bottom of the image for text. I was in two minds to frame my entry but chose not to. There''s a fair amount of CA in the lens visible at the tip/edges of the antlers and the vertical neckline., i.e. at the areas of most contrast. Not an image killer per se but it does irritate any nature tog if the lens portrays these characteristics as all your shots will have this blemish/lens flaw. Whilst I''m not of the opinion that a catchlight in the eye is required, I''ve found this to be the consensus online. Yours doesn''t have one. Publishable? Fair chance, if tied into the text.</td>', 'Beautiful work. Natural shot in natural environs. Nice light accentuation on the antlers and good exposure, DOF. There needs to be some engagement between the subject and the viewer, of which there is none. The border is common at DPC but not NG except where only one black frame is used generally at the bottom of the image for text. I was in two minds to frame my entry but chose not to. There''s a fair amount of CA in the lens visible at the tip/edges of the antlers and the vertical neckline., i.e. at the areas of most contrast. Not an image killer per se but it does irritate any nature tog if the lens portrays these characteristics as all your shots will have this blemish/lens flaw. Whilst I''m not of the opinion that a catchlight in the eye is required, I''ve found this to be the consensus online. Yours doesn''t have one. Publishable? Fair chance, if tied into the text.', '2011-07-04 03:10:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460630, 959241, 110108, '<td valign="top">a touch too over processed</td>', 'a touch too over processed', '2011-07-04 03:36:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460633, 959343, 110108, '<td valign="top">Nice color and foucs</td>', 'Nice color and foucs', '2011-07-04 03:39:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460700, 959656, 108580, '<td valign="top">Your image is fairly well exposed, looks level and has a number of elements to look at and enjoy. However is it engaging enough? Does it draw me in and tell a story? Without the benefit of text to tie it in to something I''d have to say this is a record shot only and may not reach publication, sorry.</td>', 'Your image is fairly well exposed, looks level and has a number of elements to look at and enjoy. However is it engaging enough? Does it draw me in and tell a story? Without the benefit of text to tie it in to something I''d have to say this is a record shot only and may not reach publication, sorry.', '2011-07-04 04:55:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460702, 959196, 108580, '<td valign="top">Without a dramatic splash the image, whilst being in a difficult and cold location and the effort to get here immense, is rather flat. It''s not yet telling a compelling story such as global warming. Maybe a minute later it did but your ship had moved on. Some ice fell, and I''m sure it was a moment you will never forget but what''s being shown is just too little to be momentous in the picture. NG photography to me is all about a new angle, a moment, a feeling, something thought provoking or a picture to back up the article and I don''t think this has enough of that to be accepted. ''Calve'' to me is to give birth to a calf. No doubt I''m not the first to point this out. Did you mean ''About to cave in''?<br/>ETA Post Rollover: OK I''m an ass and I learnt something new today. Apologies for the "Calve" Faux Pas. I did look it up but totally missed it.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-07-09 17:20:54.</i></td>', 'Without a dramatic splash the image, whilst being in a difficult and cold location and the effort to get here immense, is rather flat. It''s not yet telling a compelling story such as global warming. Maybe a minute later it did but your ship had moved on. Some ice fell, and I''m sure it was a moment you will never forget but what''s being shown is just too little to be momentous in the picture. NG photography to me is all about a new angle, a moment, a feeling, something thought provoking or a picture to back up the article and I don''t think this has enough of that to be accepted. ''Calve'' to me is to give birth to a calf. No doubt I''m not the first to point this out. Did you mean ''About to cave in''?ETA Post Rollover: OK I''m an ass and I learnt something new today. Apologies for the "Calve" Faux Pas. I did look it up but totally missed it.', '2011-07-04 04:56:33.000000', '2011-07-09 18:20:54.000000', 1),
(6460795, 958629, 108580, '<td valign="top">I like the backlight and the wary body language. Tricky light to get a decent overall exposure and decent s/s thus it looks a tad wobbled. I''m on the fence if it would be used or not. Would have to relate to an article I think for it to be considered.</td>', 'I like the backlight and the wary body language. Tricky light to get a decent overall exposure and decent s/s thus it looks a tad wobbled. I''m on the fence if it would be used or not. Would have to relate to an article I think for it to be considered.', '2011-07-04 09:13:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460798, 959725, 108580, '<td valign="top">With the Deer in the shade and full sunlight in the background has made even exposure very difficult. This also shows the heavy CA of the lens in the high contrast areas, such as the deer''s rump and the light green field behind it, and the edges of the antlers. However, it''s one of the few images of deer where it is actually engaging the reader however. I''m not convinced it would be used, sorry.</td>', 'With the Deer in the shade and full sunlight in the background has made even exposure very difficult. This also shows the heavy CA of the lens in the high contrast areas, such as the deer''s rump and the light green field behind it, and the edges of the antlers. However, it''s one of the few images of deer where it is actually engaging the reader however. I''m not convinced it would be used, sorry.', '2011-07-04 09:17:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460799, 959562, 61267, '<td valign="top">Wonderful bird of prey photo...10 in my book!</td>', 'Wonderful bird of prey photo...10 in my book!', '2011-07-04 09:18:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460807, 958555, 91372, '<td valign="top">imo, the border is a little too noticable</td>', 'imo, the border is a little too noticable', '2011-07-04 09:39:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460809, 959244, 91372, '<td valign="top">if you don''t work for nat geo,you should. this deserves my rarely given 10</td>', 'if you don''t work for nat geo,you should. this deserves my rarely given 10', '2011-07-04 09:40:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460811, 959422, 91372, '<td valign="top">wonderful emotion. 9</td>', 'wonderful emotion. 9', '2011-07-04 09:40:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460816, 959812, 108580, '<td valign="top">Lovely interactive image between parent and chick. Enough natural environment in the crop and the chick''s pose and both pleading eyes visible is arguably what gives this shot something more than the norm. Certainly a trait I think NG looks for. It does appear a bit OOF or slowish s/s caused some blur, lack of crispness, but is that cause for non-acceptance by NG? Debatable. My gut feel is they prefer sharp, but not always...</td>', 'Lovely interactive image between parent and chick. Enough natural environment in the crop and the chick''s pose and both pleading eyes visible is arguably what gives this shot something more than the norm. Certainly a trait I think NG looks for. It does appear a bit OOF or slowish s/s caused some blur, lack of crispness, but is that cause for non-acceptance by NG? Debatable. My gut feel is they prefer sharp, but not always...', '2011-07-04 09:45:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460818, 959019, 108580, '<td valign="top">Beautiful composition and bokeh. Fitting title. I think you let yourself down with a too slow s/s as there is blur. The tongue would have been so much better as would the overall focus. Yes, trying light, I agree. Harsh? Maybe but to be printed NG are I think very choosy, especially as they have such a huge stock library.</td>', 'Beautiful composition and bokeh. Fitting title. I think you let yourself down with a too slow s/s as there is blur. The tongue would have been so much better as would the overall focus. Yes, trying light, I agree. Harsh? Maybe but to be printed NG are I think very choosy, especially as they have such a huge stock library.', '2011-07-04 09:53:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460826, 959796, 108580, '<td valign="top">Lovely piece. NG have been known to do stories on art and culture. The white BG is not easy on the eyes. I think black is more traditional, or at least more used overall. The focus and lighting is excellent as it should be for a "still life" in "studio" work. Typical NG and printable.</td>', 'Lovely piece. NG have been known to do stories on art and culture. The white BG is not easy on the eyes. I think black is more traditional, or at least more used overall. The focus and lighting is excellent as it should be for a "still life" in "studio" work. Typical NG and printable.', '2011-07-04 10:02:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460828, 959261, 108580, '<td valign="top">It''s not an overly garish PP DPC eye candy image. Unusual in the large grassy foreground. It could be a piece on sand dune mining reclamation with the promise of rain. Of course NG have done stories about man vs nature and this could well have been used.</td>', 'It''s not an overly garish PP DPC eye candy image. Unusual in the large grassy foreground. It could be a piece on sand dune mining reclamation with the promise of rain. Of course NG have done stories about man vs nature and this could well have been used.', '2011-07-04 10:03:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460829, 959437, 108580, '<td valign="top">Nice close view of the ray. Suspiciously it is color tinted by the laminated glass of an aquarium? A bit of CA is also visible. The low light has left you with a very slow s/s and thus a blurred somewhat OOF image. It''s not terrible but I think NG would have produced something more polished.</td>', 'Nice close view of the ray. Suspiciously it is color tinted by the laminated glass of an aquarium? A bit of CA is also visible. The low light has left you with a very slow s/s and thus a blurred somewhat OOF image. It''s not terrible but I think NG would have produced something more polished.', '2011-07-04 10:03:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460835, 959655, 108580, '<td valign="top">Great documentary image. Pertaining to man''s changing the course of nature, global warming, or any other environmental issue no doubt. The heat wave has distorted the human, and I can''t judge who or what. Resident? Fire-fighter? By stander? A yellow helmet and fire-fighter gear would have elevated the image no end. Still a valid entry imo.</td>', 'Great documentary image. Pertaining to man''s changing the course of nature, global warming, or any other environmental issue no doubt. The heat wave has distorted the human, and I can''t judge who or what. Resident? Fire-fighter? By stander? A yellow helmet and fire-fighter gear would have elevated the image no end. Still a valid entry imo.', '2011-07-04 10:09:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460840, 959785, 108580, '<td valign="top">I love silhouettes. Timing and location have to be perfect. This is quite nice, the sun, the rays on the water, the fowl in the distance but I have to comment on the fisherman''s head being intersected by the water, rivers edge. It''s sometimes small attention to detail that makes an NG image stand out. Overall the exposure is good and the composition close to excellent, if only you had gotten a tad higher before shooting.</td>', 'I love silhouettes. Timing and location have to be perfect. This is quite nice, the sun, the rays on the water, the fowl in the distance but I have to comment on the fisherman''s head being intersected by the water, rivers edge. It''s sometimes small attention to detail that makes an NG image stand out. Overall the exposure is good and the composition close to excellent, if only you had gotten a tad higher before shooting.', '2011-07-04 10:13:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460843, 959671, 108580, '<td valign="top">Good composition. Difficult to get the timing and focus correct no doubt. Is it an optical illusion that overall the image appears missing red/warmth because of the overpowering purple? I think you missed the focus on the eyes of the insect. The nose and tips of the antennae appear ok. Background is great and makes the image stand out. I just think that to be "up there" insect eyes have to be focussed.</td>', 'Good composition. Difficult to get the timing and focus correct no doubt. Is it an optical illusion that overall the image appears missing red/warmth because of the overpowering purple? I think you missed the focus on the eyes of the insect. The nose and tips of the antennae appear ok. Background is great and makes the image stand out. I just think that to be "up there" insect eyes have to be focussed.', '2011-07-04 10:16:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460848, 959241, 108580, '<td valign="top">Nice quick action shot with combined human and animal interest. I fear it is too heavily processed to be acceptable by NG, judging by the haloing around the trees and unnatural skin tones.</td>', 'Nice quick action shot with combined human and animal interest. I fear it is too heavily processed to be acceptable by NG, judging by the haloing around the trees and unnatural skin tones.', '2011-07-04 10:24:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460851, 959843, 108580, '<td valign="top">Enjoyable image, with a great BG and enough sharpness on head and eyes, feathers and legs. The composition is too far to the left, breaking rules perhaps. Nothing unusual about that as NG aren''t totally formula shots. Is it telling enough of a story for NG is what you have to ask yourself before submitting it to them.</td>', 'Enjoyable image, with a great BG and enough sharpness on head and eyes, feathers and legs. The composition is too far to the left, breaking rules perhaps. Nothing unusual about that as NG aren''t totally formula shots. Is it telling enough of a story for NG is what you have to ask yourself before submitting it to them.', '2011-07-04 10:27:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460859, 959603, 108580, '<td valign="top">Sublime. No more comment necessary. Where do we sign for the release? Just hope the slight haloing is not due to PP.</td>', 'Sublime. No more comment necessary. Where do we sign for the release? Just hope the slight haloing is not due to PP.', '2011-07-04 10:35:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460867, 959547, 108580, '<td valign="top">Love it. Typical DPC eye candy, soft, colourful clouds, feathered water, the rocks. If done by ND filters, fine. Does it show actual erosion as one would see on a farm or landslides after heavy rainfall...? Sure the rocks are smooth and "eroded" by millennia of water washing over them. Making a publishing decision would rest on the relevance of the article your image is shot for. Photographically it would pass imo.</td>', 'Love it. Typical DPC eye candy, soft, colourful clouds, feathered water, the rocks. If done by ND filters, fine. Does it show actual erosion as one would see on a farm or landslides after heavy rainfall...? Sure the rocks are smooth and "eroded" by millennia of water washing over them. Making a publishing decision would rest on the relevance of the article your image is shot for. Photographically it would pass imo.', '2011-07-04 10:49:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460868, 959763, 108580, '<td valign="top">Lovely work. Not over processed it seems. Has all the right elements, slow shutter, tripod, soft filtered light, moss. Could pass for publication.</td>', 'Lovely work. Not over processed it seems. Has all the right elements, slow shutter, tripod, soft filtered light, moss. Could pass for publication.', '2011-07-04 10:50:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460871, 959737, 108580, '<td valign="top">Typical NG style documentary image. I might have tried to get higher just to be able to prevent the writing on the wall from being obscured. Great exposure and good job in getting construction workers in the shot. Engaging.</td>', 'Typical NG style documentary image. I might have tried to get higher just to be able to prevent the writing on the wall from being obscured. Great exposure and good job in getting construction workers in the shot. Engaging.', '2011-07-04 10:52:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460874, 959337, 108580, '<td valign="top">Cute little blighter''s. I remember them well. Hanging out in gum trees. Lovely, simple and natural. No tricks. I''d give it the nod for publication even if just a record shot. How unusual is it to see them in the daytime. Well spotted.</td>', 'Cute little blighter''s. I remember them well. Hanging out in gum trees. Lovely, simple and natural. No tricks. I''d give it the nod for publication even if just a record shot. How unusual is it to see them in the daytime. Well spotted.', '2011-07-04 10:59:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460877, 959700, 108580, '<td valign="top">Farms and farm implements as subjects aren''t new to NG. Showing one derelict and abandoned could well fit an article based on ever changing farmers fortunes. Image does seem a bit processed, pulling out warmth and red tones? Be wary, as they spot this very quickly and reject. Nice POV low to the ground and that UWA does add impact, as if Mother Nature will dwarf any of our attempts at altering her.</td>', 'Farms and farm implements as subjects aren''t new to NG. Showing one derelict and abandoned could well fit an article based on ever changing farmers fortunes. Image does seem a bit processed, pulling out warmth and red tones? Be wary, as they spot this very quickly and reject. Nice POV low to the ground and that UWA does add impact, as if Mother Nature will dwarf any of our attempts at altering her.', '2011-07-04 11:03:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6460887, 959396, 108580, '<td valign="top">Nice close shot, but I fear that by NOT showing the Lions surroundings there is doubt as to the authenticity of where he was photographed. As long as you do truthfully mention it then no problem. He is also too pristine to be a wild lion. One noticeable scratch on the nose ridge and a near perfect mane is sign of a pampered lion. A few wildlife togs, myself included, often try to get the natural AFRICAN bush in the shot so that there is no doubt. This can however stifle creativity, especially animal abstracts. Sure NG have done stories about captive animals so this is not a reason for them not to publish. However, it''s blurred due to a too slow shutter speed and thus camera/lens shake and would not pass their strict selection.</td>', 'Nice close shot, but I fear that by NOT showing the Lions surroundings there is doubt as to the authenticity of where he was photographed. As long as you do truthfully mention it then no problem. He is also too pristine to be a wild lion. One noticeable scratch on the nose ridge and a near perfect mane is sign of a pampered lion. A few wildlife togs, myself included, often try to get the natural AFRICAN bush in the shot so that there is no doubt. This can however stifle creativity, especially animal abstracts. Sure NG have done stories about captive animals so this is not a reason for them not to publish. However, it''s blurred due to a too slow shutter speed and thus camera/lens shake and would not pass their strict selection.', '2011-07-04 11:17:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461078, 959192, 124346, '<td valign="top">The sky looks really noisy but the sand not.  I guess you used a medium ISO and the sky wasn''t to illuminated, the sun was illuminating the sand so it didn''t look noisy, am I right?</td>', 'The sky looks really noisy but the sand not.  I guess you used a medium ISO and the sky wasn''t to illuminated, the sun was illuminating the sand so it didn''t look noisy, am I right?', '2011-07-04 16:25:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461080, 959834, 108580, '<td valign="top">Where''s the basket full of choccies? :) There''s always a huge online debate about photographing WILD life or wildlife in or around human habitation. Was it shot in your garden, a bunny park, the zoo or in the English Country (famous for their bunnies). I guess the decision rests on the editor based on the article associated with your title. It''s crisp, the eye engages me, has the obligatory catch-light, nice ROT composition. Could indeed be used for publication I think, despite the blade in front of the eye and nose, especially if doing a story on the longevity of the English rabbit.</td>', 'Where''s the basket full of choccies? :) There''s always a huge online debate about photographing WILD life or wildlife in or around human habitation. Was it shot in your garden, a bunny park, the zoo or in the English Country (famous for their bunnies). I guess the decision rests on the editor based on the article associated with your title. It''s crisp, the eye engages me, has the obligatory catch-light, nice ROT composition. Could indeed be used for publication I think, despite the blade in front of the eye and nose, especially if doing a story on the longevity of the English rabbit.', '2011-07-04 16:29:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461083, 959668, 124346, '<td valign="top">Beautiful picture, nice message and idea.  I would make a little post-processing to give the picture a nice touch, not sure what I would do, maybe some vignetting and some enhancing of the blacks.  But its really nice.</td>', 'Beautiful picture, nice message and idea.  I would make a little post-processing to give the picture a nice touch, not sure what I would do, maybe some vignetting and some enhancing of the blacks.  But its really nice.', '2011-07-04 16:33:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461088, 959347, 124346, '<td valign="top">Pier pictures are so nice, there are so many angles to take it from, sadly I don''t have one near to photograph.  Nice one.</td>', 'Pier pictures are so nice, there are so many angles to take it from, sadly I don''t have one near to photograph.  Nice one.', '2011-07-04 16:38:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461092, 959712, 124346, '<td valign="top">This is the first picture that look to me as a winner.  Nice colors and sharpness.</td>', 'This is the first picture that look to me as a winner.  Nice colors and sharpness.', '2011-07-04 16:41:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461100, 959227, 124346, '<td valign="top">Nice one, love the soft colors and the silhouette.  I say this could be a winner.</td>', 'Nice one, love the soft colors and the silhouette.  I say this could be a winner.', '2011-07-04 16:43:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461126, 958869, 108580, '<td valign="top">Well researched :) Only 14 years after NG''s first pictorial mag. The film grain effect and lack of contrast certainly appear original. The foreground firs are intensely black and seem out of place. Still you need them for depth and perspective. So it''s not modern day NG eye candy and I hope you are not ignorantly being punished for this. Kudo''s for being daring and different.</td>', 'Well researched :) Only 14 years after NG''s first pictorial mag. The film grain effect and lack of contrast certainly appear original. The foreground firs are intensely black and seem out of place. Still you need them for depth and perspective. So it''s not modern day NG eye candy and I hope you are not ignorantly being punished for this. Kudo''s for being daring and different.', '2011-07-04 17:26:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461128, 959338, 108580, '<td valign="top">Certainly a valid culture shot. NG images aren''t all sharp. Motion blur used in their photography is common place. This tells a story, the lack of adequate delivery vehicles or money to pay for it, and that''s sometimes all that''s needed to fill the spaces between the text. NG make us sit up and think.</td>', 'Certainly a valid culture shot. NG images aren''t all sharp. Motion blur used in their photography is common place. This tells a story, the lack of adequate delivery vehicles or money to pay for it, and that''s sometimes all that''s needed to fill the spaces between the text. NG make us sit up and think.', '2011-07-04 17:32:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461143, 958555, 108580, '<td valign="top">I''m hard pressed to comment on your image. I''m trying to do them all. Without being too harsh I''d like to say that when shooting animals, especially for a magazine of such photographic quality of NG, you need to get your exposure right. Shooting dark animals or birds is very difficult. Balance the fur and eyes to get definition but not blow out the rest of the subject. NG do allow dodge and burn, it''s one of the few PP techniques that they do. So, when shooting animal AND environment shoot in RAW, spot meter the GREEN LEAVES/FOLIAGE, lock the exposure using AE-L, recompose to him and shoot. Try it and you wont get a washed out look. Next step, get the animal to engage YOU, or wait till he does. Try zoom in on his face and get a full portrait, with a catch light in the eyes if you can. there''s no harm in shooting in the zoo or animal park. It''s perfect to get your technique right before facing a Grizzly in Yellowstone :)</td>', 'I''m hard pressed to comment on your image. I''m trying to do them all. Without being too harsh I''d like to say that when shooting animals, especially for a magazine of such photographic quality of NG, you need to get your exposure right. Shooting dark animals or birds is very difficult. Balance the fur and eyes to get definition but not blow out the rest of the subject. NG do allow dodge and burn, it''s one of the few PP techniques that they do. So, when shooting animal AND environment shoot in RAW, spot meter the GREEN LEAVES/FOLIAGE, lock the exposure using AE-L, recompose to him and shoot. Try it and you wont get a washed out look. Next step, get the animal to engage YOU, or wait till he does. Try zoom in on his face and get a full portrait, with a catch light in the eyes if you can. there''s no harm in shooting in the zoo or animal park. It''s perfect to get your technique right before facing a Grizzly in Yellowstone :)', '2011-07-04 17:43:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461149, 959841, 108580, '<td valign="top">Wow. You got really close! A nice attempt. Did you use a tripod or was it handheld? A 70-300mm or a prime? Something shorter like a 55-200mm and digitally cropped? There is very little DOF in this image, less than a few mm''s from eye to midline of the beak. I fear that the shutter speed was possibly too low to make it crisp and sharp. On a compositional note, if you could place him to the right of the image with space to the side he is looking, it would be more appealing. It might be used because it is an unusual sighting, but the lack of crisp focus and cramped crop might be it''s downfall.</td>', 'Wow. You got really close! A nice attempt. Did you use a tripod or was it handheld? A 70-300mm or a prime? Something shorter like a 55-200mm and digitally cropped? There is very little DOF in this image, less than a few mm''s from eye to midline of the beak. I fear that the shutter speed was possibly too low to make it crisp and sharp. On a compositional note, if you could place him to the right of the image with space to the side he is looking, it would be more appealing. It might be used because it is an unusual sighting, but the lack of crisp focus and cramped crop might be it''s downfall.', '2011-07-04 17:48:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461154, 959434, 108580, '<td valign="top">This is an appealing image. They are damn lazy those big boys. To catch the late light and "golden up" &amp; intensify the eyes is a nice touch. I''m taking a flyer here and may end up with egg on my face; You''ve rotated the image clockwise? This would be a terribly uncomfortable and unnatural position for the lion to lie. Maybe not impossible but I fear it would be challenge by NG.</td>', 'This is an appealing image. They are damn lazy those big boys. To catch the late light and "golden up" & intensify the eyes is a nice touch. I''m taking a flyer here and may end up with egg on my face; You''ve rotated the image clockwise? This would be a terribly uncomfortable and unnatural position for the lion to lie. Maybe not impossible but I fear it would be challenge by NG.', '2011-07-04 17:53:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461158, 959779, 108580, '<td valign="top">It''s a nice close shot of this colourful bird, with no distracting leaves or twigs blocking any part of it''s body. Did you digitally crop? That''s fine in terms of what NG allows when submitting, but It really looks like you lost definition and in the process got a lot of noise. There also seems to be traits of plugin post processing visible in the multiple layered lines shown at the edge of the leaves going to blue sky. If that where true, NG would say no I think.</td>', 'It''s a nice close shot of this colourful bird, with no distracting leaves or twigs blocking any part of it''s body. Did you digitally crop? That''s fine in terms of what NG allows when submitting, but It really looks like you lost definition and in the process got a lot of noise. There also seems to be traits of plugin post processing visible in the multiple layered lines shown at the edge of the leaves going to blue sky. If that where true, NG would say no I think.', '2011-07-04 17:57:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461167, 959752, 108580, '<td valign="top">They really do look pissed off don''t they? Really engaging image. Of course I can''t pick if it''s a non-captive bird or not. Still, NG has used both and I think if all else pans out would use this. Depends on the article. The sharp eyes are what make this image. The shallow DOF makes it pop. What I can''t seem to pinpoint is why the feathers immediately near the eyes and at the same plane seem less focused. Were the eyes only sharpened? Is it a trait of JPG compression? I could be way off base here and that''s OK. Critiquing is far easier after roll over...</td>', 'They really do look pissed off don''t they? Really engaging image. Of course I can''t pick if it''s a non-captive bird or not. Still, NG has used both and I think if all else pans out would use this. Depends on the article. The sharp eyes are what make this image. The shallow DOF makes it pop. What I can''t seem to pinpoint is why the feathers immediately near the eyes and at the same plane seem less focused. Were the eyes only sharpened? Is it a trait of JPG compression? I could be way off base here and that''s OK. Critiquing is far easier after roll over...', '2011-07-04 18:03:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461175, 958739, 108580, '<td valign="top">Interesting choice. No humans, just the boat. What is the tog trying to tell me? I can''t tell! Perhaps abandonment, fishing crisis? Fish stocks story? Lunchtime? I feel that NG images must tell me a story. Yes, not all will but it''s what I''ve come to expect after reading it for many years. I''m at a loss with this one.</td>', 'Interesting choice. No humans, just the boat. What is the tog trying to tell me? I can''t tell! Perhaps abandonment, fishing crisis? Fish stocks story? Lunchtime? I feel that NG images must tell me a story. Yes, not all will but it''s what I''ve come to expect after reading it for many years. I''m at a loss with this one.', '2011-07-04 18:06:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461181, 959430, 108580, '<td valign="top">Classy image, for a fly :) You have a got one superb eye, and the patience. Everything here seems just right to me. Perfect exposure and composition. Sharp eye, iridescent body, sharp hairs, smooooooth background and a few very very tiny flowers to complete the picture. Submit to them now!</td>', 'Classy image, for a fly :) You have a got one superb eye, and the patience. Everything here seems just right to me. Perfect exposure and composition. Sharp eye, iridescent body, sharp hairs, smooooooth background and a few very very tiny flowers to complete the picture. Submit to them now!', '2011-07-04 18:09:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461252, 959688, 41267, '<td valign="top">i say a 10. Lovely pic!!</td>', 'i say a 10. Lovely pic!!', '2011-07-04 18:48:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6461336, 959834, 124815, '<td valign="top">This is looking just like the model Durer had!<br/>I cannot find the exact work but look at these plants, the rabbit is perfect also<br/><a href="//www.albrecht-durer.org/The-So-Called-Great-Piece-Of-Turf-large.html" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.albrecht-durer.org/The-So-Called-Great-Piece-Of-Turf-large.html</a></td>', 'This is looking just like the model Durer had!I cannot find the exact work but look at these plants, the rabbit is perfect also//www.albrecht-durer.org/The-So-Called-Great-Piece-Of-Turf-large.html', '2011-07-04 20:50:37.000000', NULL, 1),
