(6469758, 958392, 112739, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LydiaToo:</b></div><hr/><i> I don''t think bluebirds are concerned... since they have only instincts and not feelings, but this is beautiful.   Love the composition.<br/> <br/>I may or may not be voting, so please do not equate my comment with any score. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>How can you state that Bluebirds are not concerned or that they do not have feelings? Why can''t the title mean a "General Sense" from anyone who has concern for the forests? What sort of shallow, self absorbed human thinking is that?  I would imagine that if a horse or a dog has feelings, then a Blue bird would too. Does the size of your brain dictate whether a creature has feelings?  I would image a Blue bird would have a certain amount of satifaction from raising thier chicks. And if the environment has changed because of things beyond thier control, it would affect them and they would be forced to build thier homes in other places. They do have a certain instincts, but they are not machines. This image should have been accepted better than it was in this challenge. I was totally surprised to see it finish where it did.</td>', 'Originally posted by LydiaToo: I don''t think bluebirds are concerned... since they have only instincts and not feelings, but this is beautiful.   Love the composition. I may or may not be voting, so please do not equate my comment with any score.   How can you state that Bluebirds are not concerned or that they do not have feelings? Why can''t the title mean a "General Sense" from anyone who has concern for the forests? What sort of shallow, self absorbed human thinking is that?  I would imagine that if a horse or a dog has feelings, then a Blue bird would too. Does the size of your brain dictate whether a creature has feelings?  I would image a Blue bird would have a certain amount of satifaction from raising thier chicks. And if the environment has changed because of things beyond thier control, it would affect them and they would be forced to build thier homes in other places. They do have a certain instincts, but they are not machines. This image should have been accepted better than it was in this challenge. I was totally surprised to see it finish where it did.', '2011-07-13 16:36:23.000000', NULL, 0),
