(6655354, 959334, 28742, '<td valign="top">Hey, just saw this, Jeff. Funny, I have been in Seattle for 21+ years and have not been to the underground. My wife really wants to go. I am wondering how much (non-flash) photo ops there are on the tour?<br/> <br/>Great image, btw. Reminds me of Beneath the Planet of the Apes. But then most things remind me of a PotA movie. ;-)</td>', 'Hey, just saw this, Jeff. Funny, I have been in Seattle for 21+ years and have not been to the underground. My wife really wants to go. I am wondering how much (non-flash) photo ops there are on the tour? Great image, btw. Reminds me of Beneath the Planet of the Apes. But then most things remind me of a PotA movie. ;-)', '2012-01-26 04:05:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(6661499, 959603, 108580, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by MAK:</b></div><hr/><i> I would relish the chance to visit there... I had an uncle in SA once, dunno where he is now though. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Unfortunately the bottom half of Kruger got flooded 3 weeks ago, but true to SA grit, most of it is open again and repairs have already started. Uncle or not, give me an early shout and either go together (30 years experience in the Kruger) or I''ll give you some tips :) I''m often there a few times a year. Remember it''s southern hemisphere so work out the seasons. You need at least a full 7 days there, more if you can afford it. Camping is the most affordable way and doable. PM me if you like.</td>', 'Originally posted by MAK: I would relish the chance to visit there... I had an uncle in SA once, dunno where he is now though.  Unfortunately the bottom half of Kruger got flooded 3 weeks ago, but true to SA grit, most of it is open again and repairs have already started. Uncle or not, give me an early shout and either go together (30 years experience in the Kruger) or I''ll give you some tips :) I''m often there a few times a year. Remember it''s southern hemisphere so work out the seasons. You need at least a full 7 days there, more if you can afford it. Camping is the most affordable way and doable. PM me if you like.', '2012-02-02 02:17:47.000000', NULL, 0),
